  <main class="section">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:760px;">
      <h1 class="section-title">JWT Tokens: How They Work and How to Use Them Safely</h1>
      <p style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:0.9rem;margin-bottom:24px;">Published: August 10, 2026</p>
      <article style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.8;">
        <p>JSON Web Tokens (JWT) are a compact, URL-safe way to transmit claims between parties. They're widely used for authentication and information exchange in modern web applications.</p>
        <h2 style="font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--text);margin-top:32px;margin-bottom:12px;">Structure</h2>
        <p>A JWT consists of three parts separated by dots: header, payload, and signature. The header specifies the algorithm (e.g., HS256). The payload contains claims (data). The signature verifies the token's authenticity.</p>
        <h2 style="font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--text);margin-top:32px;margin-bottom:12px;">How It Works</h2>
        <p>When a user logs in, the server creates a JWT with user claims and signs it with a secret key. The client stores the token and sends it in the Authorization header for subsequent requests. The server verifies the signature before processing.</p>
        <h2 style="font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--text);margin-top:32px;margin-bottom:12px;">Security Best Practices</h2>
        <p>Always use HTTPS to prevent token interception. Store tokens in HttpOnly cookies for web apps, not localStorage. Set short expiration times (15-60 minutes). Use refresh tokens for long-lived sessions. Never store sensitive data in the payload — it's only base64-encoded, not encrypted.</p>
        <h2 style="font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--text);margin-top:32px;margin-bottom:12px;">Common Mistakes</h2>
        <p>Using weak secrets, storing tokens in localStorage (vulnerable to XSS), not validating the signature, and accepting tokens without checking the issuer (iss) or audience (aud) claims.</p>
      </article>

      <div style="margin-top:32px;padding-top:24px;border-top:1px solid var(--border);">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:12px;">Related Tools</h3>
