      </div>

      <section class="faq" style="margin-top:32px;">
        <h3>Frequently Asked Questions</h3>
        <details>
          <summary>Is JWT encrypted?</summary>
          <div class="faq-body">No. JWT is base64url-encoded, not encrypted. Anyone can decode the payload. Use JWE for encrypted tokens.</div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Should I use JWT for sessions?</summary>
          <div class="faq-body">JWTs are stateless, which makes them popular for APIs. For web apps, consider the trade-offs: no server-side session storage vs. difficult revocation.</div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What algorithms are recommended?</summary>
          <div class="faq-body">Use RS256 (asymmetric) when possible. If using HS256 (symmetric), ensure your secret is long and randomly generated.</div>
        </details>
      </section>
